''la xunre poi pendo mi''

This means "Red Friend of Mine", where the whole phrase is the name. If you want to say "Red who is my friend (as opposed to someone else named "Red")", when only "Red" is the name, it must be ''la xunre ku poi pendo mi''. A relative phrase that comes before the ''ku'' in a name is part of the name, and one that comes after is not. See ''((The Complete Lojban Language))'', [http://www.lojban.org/files/reference-grammar/chap8.html#s6|chapter 8.6] (examples 10 and 11, p. 179).

----

Just because you can elide them in 99.9% of cases doesn't mean that you can't forget about your friends, the ((elidable terminator))s.
